1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,263
<font color="#000000">VideoComposer, from Alibaba and Ant Group,</font>

2
00:00:03,343 --> 00:00:07,055
<font color="#000000">makes video generation controllable through composition.</font>

3
00:00:07,135 --> 00:00:11,387
<font color="#000000">Users combine textual, spatial, and temporal
conditions at once.</font>

4
00:00:11,467 --> 00:00:17,006
<font color="#000000">Its key ideas: motion vectors from compressed video
as an explicit temporal signal,</font>

5
00:00:17,086 --> 00:00:24,318
<font color="#000000">and a unified Spatio-Temporal Condition encoder
that fuses diverse controls while keeping frames consistent,</font>

6
00:00:24,398 --> 00:00:28,380
<font color="#000000">from text and sketches to reference video or simple
strokes.</font>

7
00:00:28,760 --> 00:00:34,401
<font color="#000000">Diffusion models made image generation highly
controllable, but video is much harder.</font>

8
00:00:34,481 --> 00:00:39,314
<font color="#000000">Video adds a temporal axis: motion patterns vary
enormously across clips,</font>

9
00:00:39,394 --> 00:00:43,150
<font color="#000000">and every frame must stay consistent with its neighbours.</font>

10
00:00:43,230 --> 00:00:49,544
<font color="#000000">Reusing the spatial controls designed for images
gives no reliable handle on temporal dynamics,</font>

11
00:00:49,624 --> 00:00:53,380
<font color="#000000">so controllable video synthesis stayed an open challenge.</font>

12
00:00:53,760 --> 00:00:58,728
<font color="#000000">To control a video, you must control its motion,
not only its appearance.</font>

13
00:00:58,808 --> 00:01:01,286
<font color="#000000">The authors' insight: motion vectors,</font>

14
00:01:01,366 --> 00:01:06,472
<font color="#000000">computed inside compressed video to encode
inter-frame change, are a cheap,</font>

15
00:01:06,552 --> 00:01:09,376
<font color="#000000">explicit description of temporal dynamics.</font>

16
00:01:09,456 --> 00:01:14,355
<font color="#000000">Turning them into a control signal lets users
prescribe how things move.</font>

17
00:01:14,435 --> 00:01:19,541
<font color="#000000">But mixing them with sketches, depth, and images
naively hurts consistency,</font>

18
00:01:19,621 --> 00:01:22,860
<font color="#000000">motivating a unified encoder for space and time.</font>

19
00:01:23,240 --> 00:01:26,446
<font color="#000000">VideoComposer makes three contributions.</font>

20
00:01:26,526 --> 00:01:29,732
<font color="#000000">First,</font>

21
00:01:29,812 --> 00:01:33,018
<font color="#000000">it frames video generation as compositional: a user
supplies any subset of textual,</font>

22
00:01:33,098 --> 00:01:36,304
<font color="#000000">spatial, and temporal conditions,</font>

23
00:01:36,384 --> 00:01:39,590
<font color="#000000">and the model recomposes a video obeying all of them.</font>

24
00:01:39,670 --> 00:01:42,876
<font color="#000000">Second,</font>

25
00:01:42,956 --> 00:01:46,162
<font color="#000000">it introduces motion vectors from compressed video
as an explicit temporal control signal.</font>

26
00:01:46,242 --> 00:01:49,448
<font color="#000000">Third, it proposes the Spatio-Temporal Condition encoder,</font>

27
00:01:49,528 --> 00:01:52,734
<font color="#000000">a lightweight module that turns every sequential
condition into a shared representation</font>

28
00:01:52,814 --> 00:01:56,020
<font color="#000000">while boosting temporal consistency.</font>

29
00:01:56,400 --> 00:02:02,388
<font color="#000000">VideoComposer is a latent diffusion model that
denoises video in a compressed latent space.</font>

30
00:02:02,468 --> 00:02:07,522
<font color="#000000">Each training video is decomposed into three
families of conditions, textual,</font>

31
00:02:07,602 --> 00:02:10,122
<font color="#000000">spatial, and temporal, combined freely.</font>

32
00:02:10,202 --> 00:02:14,189
<font color="#000000">Sequential conditions like motion vectors, depth
maps, masks,</font>

33
00:02:14,269 --> 00:02:21,857
<font color="#000000">and sketches all pass through one shared
STC-encoder: two convolutions and pooling capture local spatial structure,</font>

34
00:02:21,937 --> 00:02:25,591
<font color="#000000">then a temporal Transformer models change across frames.</font>

35
00:02:25,671 --> 00:02:30,192
<font color="#000000">Encoded conditions are summed and concatenated with
the noisy latent,</font>

36
00:02:30,272 --> 00:02:33,592
<font color="#000000">while text and style enter through cross-attention.</font>

37
00:02:33,672 --> 00:02:35,459
<font color="#000000">Training runs in two stages,</font>

38
00:02:35,539 --> 00:02:39,660
<font color="#000000">and inference uses DDIM sampling with
classifier-free guidance.</font>

39
00:02:40,040 --> 00:02:44,528
<font color="#000000">VideoComposer is trained on two public datasets:
WebVid-10M,</font>

40
00:02:44,608 --> 00:02:49,097
<font color="#000000">about ten million video-caption pairs from the web,
and LAION-400M,</font>

41
00:02:49,177 --> 00:02:53,665
<font color="#000000">CLIP-filtered image-caption pairs for visual quality.</font>

42
00:02:53,745 --> 00:02:58,233
<font color="#000000">For evaluation,</font>

43
00:02:58,313 --> 00:03:02,802
<font color="#000000">the authors report text-to-video on MSR-VTT using
Fréchet Video Distance and CLIP similarity,</font>

44
00:03:02,882 --> 00:03:07,370
<font color="#000000">and measure motion controllability on a thousand
caption-video pairs with a dedicated motion-control error.</font>

45
00:03:07,750 --> 00:03:10,952
<font color="#000000">On MSR-VTT,</font>

46
00:03:11,032 --> 00:03:14,234
<font color="#000000">VideoComposer achieves a Fréchet Video Distance of
five hundred eighty and a CLIP similarity</font>

47
00:03:14,314 --> 00:03:17,517
<font color="#000000">of zero point two nine three two,</font>

48
00:03:17,597 --> 00:03:20,799
<font color="#000000">zero-shot.</font>

49
00:03:20,879 --> 00:03:24,081
<font color="#000000">That is competitive with leading text-to-video systems,</font>

50
00:03:24,161 --> 00:03:27,363
<font color="#000000">and it improves over the model's first-stage pre-training,</font>

51
00:03:27,443 --> 00:03:30,646
<font color="#000000">which scored eight hundred three.</font>

52
00:03:30,726 --> 00:03:33,928
<font color="#000000">So adding compositional, multi-condition control
costs nothing in quality,</font>

53
00:03:34,008 --> 00:03:37,210
<font color="#000000">while videos follow the sketches, depth, motion,
and styles users provide.</font>

54
00:03:37,590 --> 00:03:40,700
<font color="#000000">The ablations isolate where control originates.</font>

55
00:03:40,780 --> 00:03:45,452
<font color="#000000">Using only text gives a motion-control error of
four point zero three.</font>

56
00:03:45,532 --> 00:03:50,747
<font color="#000000">Adding motion vectors as a temporal condition drops
it to two point six seven,</font>

57
00:03:50,827 --> 00:03:56,449
<font color="#000000">and enabling the Spatio-Temporal Condition encoder
lowers it to two point one eight.</font>

58
00:03:56,529 --> 00:03:59,571
<font color="#000000">Both matter: motion vectors supply the signal,</font>

59
00:03:59,651 --> 00:04:02,490
<font color="#000000">and the STC-encoder makes the model use it.</font>

60
00:04:02,870 --> 00:04:06,520
<font color="#000000">A few numbers capture the impact.</font>

61
00:04:06,600 --> 00:04:10,250
<font color="#000000">On MSR-VTT,</font>

62
00:04:10,330 --> 00:04:13,980
<font color="#000000">VideoComposer scores a Fréchet Video Distance of
five hundred eighty and a CLIP similarity</font>

63
00:04:14,060 --> 00:04:17,710
<font color="#000000">of zero point two nine three two.</font>

64
00:04:17,790 --> 00:04:21,440
<font color="#000000">Its motion-control error falls to two point one eight,</font>

65
00:04:21,520 --> 00:04:25,170
<font color="#000000">versus four point zero three for a text-only baseline.</font>

66
00:04:25,250 --> 00:04:28,900
<font color="#000000">And all is learned from two datasets, WebVid-10M
and LAION-400M.</font>

67
00:04:29,280 --> 00:04:35,382
<font color="#000000">The takeaway: video generation becomes more
controllable when you treat a video as a composition</font>

68
00:04:35,462 --> 00:04:38,538
<font color="#000000">of conditions and give motion an explicit signal.</font>

69
00:04:38,618 --> 00:04:44,720
<font color="#000000">VideoComposer combines compressed-video motion
vectors with a Spatio-Temporal Condition encoder,</font>

70
00:04:44,800 --> 00:04:50,130
<font color="#000000">so users steer content and motion together, from
text, sketches, and depth to masks,</font>

71
00:04:50,210 --> 00:04:54,380
<font color="#000000">reference videos, or two strokes, while keeping
frames consistent.</font>
